<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guglielmo Gonzaga, Duke of Mantua</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1538–1587</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guglielmo Gonzaga (1538–1587) was Duke of Mantua from 1550 and became Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montferrat">Montferrat</a> when Emperor Maximilian II raised it to a duchy in 1574. Despite a hunched back he proved a careful administrator who curbed the power of the nobility of Montferrat. A keen musician and composer, he built the basilica of Santa Barbara in Mantua as the court church.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guglielmo-gonzaga-duke-of-mantua.jpg" alt="Guglielmo Gonzaga, Duke of Mantua" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified painter · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Guglielmo_I_Gonzaga.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
